      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Natural orifice transluminal endoscopic surgery (NOTES) is a newer field of endoscopic surgery that allows for scarless treatment of pathologic entities, using novel transluminal approaches. There has been a shift of focus from a clinical and research standpoint from the development and dissemination of \"first-generation\" NOTES procedures to \"new NOTES\" procedures that traverse the mucosa of luminal structures, yet do not stray far into the peritoneal cavity. It has been a challenge to find appropriate and effective ways to train gastroenterologists and surgeons in these novel approaches. We review the importance of simulation in training and discuss available simulation options."
      },
